The shopkeeper gives me the new SIM card.
He says, "Madam, this is your new number."
I take the SIM card.
I look at my new phone number.
I read it aloud.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five."
"Four, three, two, one, zero."
This is my Indian number.
I read the number again.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five..."
"...four, three, two, one, zero."
Now I memorize my number.
I put the SIM card in my phone.
My phone turns on.
I say, "Thank you, dada."
The shopkeeper smiles.
Now I have an Indian phone number.
I am very happy.
